 curveVertex ( 10 , 10 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 10 , 10 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 15 , 40 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 40 , 35 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 25 , 15 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 15 , 25 ) ; 
 curveVertex ( 15 , 25 ) ; 
 endShape ( ) ;
``` |```
beginShape ( ) ; 

 splineVertex ( 10 , 10 ) ; 
 splineVertex ( 15 , 40 ) ; 
 splineVertex ( 40 , 35 ) ; 
 splineVertex ( 25 , 15 ) ; 
 splineVertex ( 15 , 25 ) ; 

 endShape ( ) ;
``` |

Similarly, `endShape(CLOSE)` (or `endContour(CLOSE)` if you're in a contour) will cause a spline to smoothly loop back on itself so you no longer need to double up any points:

